    // PlayStation SPU hardware-canonical 512-entry gaussian table (no$psx). Unlike
    // the interleaved SNES-logged `gauss` table above, this is the curve the real
    // PSX SPU uses: a single rising half indexed 0x000..0x1FF (peak 0x59B3 at
    // 0x1FF). The four taps for fractional index i (0..0xFF) are gauss512[0x0FF-i],
    // gauss512[0x1FF-i], gauss512[0x100+i], gauss512[0x000+i] applied oldest..newest,
    // each product right-shifted 15 (SAR) before summing. The four coefficients sum
    // to 0x7F7F..0x7F81 (not exactly 0x8000), giving the hardware's slight ~0.4%
    // attenuation - the `gauss` table above sums >0x8000 and runs over-unity, which
    // is the steady-state value error this table fixes. Voice interpolation uses
    // this; XA (xa.cc) still uses the legacy `gauss` table (no golden gate yet).
